  "description": "MINKUT crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C36 H78 Dy6 N12 O36,3(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.767-3.780 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 108.78-111.48°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C42H84N15O36Dy6. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
